    <decisions>
        <description>Check if incoming email is for a case that has already been closed, if yes, stop the process, as notification will be handled via different flow (Email Message - Re-Open Case &amp; Notify Owner)</description>
        <name>Status_Check</name>
        <label>Status Check</label>
        <locationX>440</locationX>
        <locationY>647</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Check_Record_Type</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>All Open Statuses</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Closed_Status</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Parent.IsClosed</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <label>Closed Status</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Modified July, 2026 - remove the paths for Ops team related to General Question cases as Omni Channel is being implemented. Going forward, this flow will only be responsible for Minifleet record type cases.

Ths flow will be used to notify case owner about new incoming email from a customer against their case. In instances where case hasnt been assigned to a queue, a group of people will be notified.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>Formula to check if case is new</description>
        <name>isNewCase</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>DATETIMEVALUE({!$Record.CreatedDate}) - {!Get_Case.CreatedDate} &lt;= (1/1440)</expression>
    </formulas>
